course: dictionary
lesson: 14463
title: Parr: a young fish in a river
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can name a stage in a life. «The young parr darted between the stones in the river.» The words river and darted give clues: a parr lives in a river and moves fast, so a parr is a fish. The sentence tells you what kind of thing it is, even before you know the word.
explain: Parr is a noun, so it names a thing. Read on for more clues. «Dark parr marks on its sides helped it hide among the pebbles.» Marks that help a creature hide show you it is small and needs to stay safe. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: a young fish in a river still makes sense there.
explain: A word can also tell you where something is in its life. «After the parr stage, the fish becomes a smolt and swims to the sea.» The word stage shows that parr is one step in a life cycle, and smolt is the next step. Put the stages in order and the word makes sense.
fact: A parr is a young salmon or trout.
fact: A parr lives in a river for its first year or two of life.
fact: A parr swims to the sea later in its life.
fact: «Parr marks» are dark marks on a parr's sides that help it hide.
fact: In a salmon's life cycle, the order is egg, alevin, fry, parr, smolt, then adult.
exercise: «The young parr darted between the stones in the river.» What is a parr? | A bird that sings by the sea | A large fish that lives only in the sea | *A young salmon or trout living in a river | A type of river rock
exercise: «Dark parr marks on its sides helped it hide among the pebbles.» What are parr marks for? | To make the fish swim faster | To feed the fish | *To help the fish hide | To show the fish is ready for the sea
exercise: «After the parr stage, the fish becomes a smolt and swims to the sea.» Find and copy one word that names a stage of the fish's life. | *smolt | river | sea | pebbles
test: «Scientists counted every parr in the stream.» What does parr mean here? | A bird that nests near streams | A grown salmon that has swum back from the sea | *A young salmon or trout in a river | A kind of water weed
test: In the life cycle of a salmon, which stage comes straight after parr? | *Smolt | Adult | Egg | Alevin
exam: «Dark parr marks on its sides help the young fish hide in the river.» Which clue tells you parr is a fish, not a bird? | It sounds like the word parrot | It hides from birds, so it must be a bird | *It lives in a river and has marks on its sides like a fish | It is a short word
